4,4,4,4,4],[4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4]]}]},"teaching_variant":"canonical","teacher_models":["claude-opus-5-5"],"explanation":"## How the puzzle works\n\n**What the grid is made of.** Every input contains a row of identical \"plus-ish\" shapes (3 rows tall, 5 wide). They stand in columns at x 3–7, 9–13, 15–19 and 21–25, with the bottom shape on rows 25–27. Some columns are stacks of 2 or 3 copies, one above the other with a pitch of 4 rows. The bottom row of the grid, row 29, holds 5-wide marker bars. Each bar sits directly under one column, and every bar is colour 2 or colour 3.\n\n**What the markers do.** I compared each marked column in the input with the same column in the output:\n\n| pair | marker 2 → column | effect | marker 3 → column | effect |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | colour 9, height 2 | recoloured to 5 | colour 1, height 1 | grows to 3 (+2) |\n| 2 | colour 6, height 1 | recoloured to 5 | colour 0, height 3 | grows to 4 (+1) |\n| 3 | colour 3, height 3 | recoloured to 5 | colour 2, height 3 | grows to 6 (+3) |\n\n- A **2-marker** always recolours its whole column to 5 and leaves the height alone.\n- A **3-marker** stacks extra copies of the shape on top of its column, keeping the column's colour.\n- The number of copies added always equals the height of the 2-marked (recoloured) column: 2, 1 and 3 in the three pairs.\n- In every output the marker bars are erased to background.\n\n**Applying it to the test.** There are two 2-markers, under the colour-1 and colour-9 columns. Each of those columns has height 1, so both become colour 5. The single 3-marker sits under the colour-8 column. I take the extension as the sum of the recoloured heights, 1 + 1 = 2, so the 8 column grows from 1 to 3 shapes. Finally all marker bars are erased.\n\nUsing a sum is my generalisation, because every train pair has only one 2-marker. Nothing in the train pairs confirms how two 2-markers should combine.\n\n**Construction stages emitted:**\n1. Erase the marker row.\n2. Recolour each 2-marked column.\n3. Stamp the new shape copies upward on each 3-marked column, using the same 4-row pitch as the existing stacks.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    h, w = g.shape\n    bg = background(g)\n    out = g.copy()\n    # markers on the bottom row\n    markers = []\n    row = g[h - 1]\n    x = 0\n    while x < w:\n        if row[x] != bg:\n            c = row[x]; x0 = x\n            while x < w and row[x] == c:\n                x += 1\n            markers.append((int(c), x0, x - 1))\n        else:\n            x += 1\n    out[h - 1, :] = bg\n    emit(out, \"Erase the marker bars on the bottom row.\")\n\n    objs = [o for o in objects(g[:h - 1], bg=bg)]\n\n    def column(x0, x1):\n        return sorted([o for o in objs if o[\"box\"][1] == x0 and o[\"box\"][3] == x1],\n                      key=lambda o: o[\"box\"][0])\n\n    # recolour 2-marked columns, total their heights\n    total = 0\n    for c, x0, x1 in markers:\n        if c == 2:\n            col = column(x0, x1)\n            total += len(col)\n            for o in col:\n                for (y, xx) in o[\"cells\"]:\n                    out[y, xx] = 5\n            emit(out, f\"Column at x={x0}-{x1} is marked by a 2-bar: recolour its {len(col)} shape(s) to 5.\")\n\n    # extend 3-marked columns upward by total copies\n    for c, x0, x1 in markers:\n        if c == 3:\n            col = column(x0, x1)\n            if not col:\n                continue\n            top = col[0]\n            sh = top[\"box\"][2] - top[\"box\"][0] + 1\n            pitch = (col[1][\"box\"][0] - col[0][\"box\"][0]) if len(col) > 1 else sh + 1\n            for k in range(1, total + 1):\n                dy = -pitch * k\n                for (y, xx) in top[\"cells\"]:\n                    if 0 <= y + dy < h:\n                        out[y + dy, xx] = top[\"colour\"]\n            emit(out, f\"Column at x={x0}-{x1} is marked by a 3-bar: stack {total} more copies on top.\")\n\n    emit(out, \"Final grid.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"recolour":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"| 1 | colour 9, height 2 | recoloured to 5 | colour 1, height 1 | grows to 3 (+2) |"},{"source":"final explanation","text":"| 2 | colour 6, height 1 | recoloured to 5 | colour 0, height 3 | grows to 4 (+1) |"},{"source":"final explanation","text":"| 3 | colour 3, height 3 | recoloured to 5 | colour 2, height 3 | grows to 6 (+3) |"}],"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Stamp the new shape copies upward on each 3-marked column, using the same 4-row pitch as the existing stacks."}],"count":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- The number of copies added always equals the height of the 2-marked (recoloured) column: 2, 1 and 3 in the three pairs."}],"layers":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- A **3-marker** stacks extra copies of the shape on top of its column, keeping the column's colour."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Column at x=15-19 is marked by a 3-bar: stack 2 more copies on top."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Column at x=3-7 is marked by a 3-bar: stack 1 more copies on top."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"1d2ca72c643ddf33e4c25dc745c252b98449c4fd01619a76f458b7386f5b6e3d","task_sha256":"d8c67c15c4f56525175c022e0d5ed73073c08b2a6f363ead14d0ddeec9d07c0c","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
